.TH BTX-MODELD 1 "September 2026" "BTX 0.34.7" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
btx-modeld \- BTX Native Model Network helper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B btx-modeld
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Isolated helper for the BTX Native Model Network. A BTX node already has
compute; this process acquires and optionally seeds models. Inference is
local after acquisition. This is not a remote inference marketplace and has
no monetary consensus authority.
.PP
If this process exits, monetary BTX continues independently.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-decode=\fIuri\fR
Decode a
.B btx://
resource and exit.
.TP
.B \-modeldir=\fIdir\fR
Catalog and piece store (never wallet or chainstate).
.TP
.B \-modelstorage=\fIsize\fR
Payload quota (bytes or
.BR 80GiB ).
Default 0: no payload, no seeding, no preserve-rare.
.TP
.B \-modelcache=\fIsize\fR
Alias of
.BR \-modelstorage .
.TP
.B \-modelseed=\fIauto|manual|off\fR
Demand-seed policy. Default
.B auto
once storage is allocated: an intentional import or retrieve is re-advertised.
.TP
.B \-modelseedupondownload=\fI0|1\fR
Alias of
.B \-modelseed
(1 = auto, 0 = off).
.TP
.B \-modelpreserverare
Opt-in fetch of qualified under-replicated models into spare quota.
.TP
.B \-modeluploadlimit=\fIbps\fR
Aggregate serving cap in bytes/s. 0 means existing connection ceilings only.
.TP
.B \-modelbind=\fIip:port\fR
PQ1 TLS listen address. Empty means unix RPC only.
.TP
.B \-modelrpcsocket=\fIpath\fR
Unix JSON-RPC socket.
.TP
.B \-modeltransport=pq1
Only accepted value; anything else fail-closes.
.TP
.B \-modelfollowpeers=\fI0|1\fR
Follow FREE catalogs of \-modelpeer / addmodelnode / PEX contacts into spare quota (default 1).
.TP
.B \-modelpeer=\fIhost:port\fR
Model-plane bootstrap contact (repeatable). Not monetary addnode.
.TP
.B \-modelseednode=\fIhost:port\fR
Alias of \-modelpeer.
.TP
.B \-modelhost
Serve seeded artifacts over PQ1.
.TP
.B \-modelrelay
CPU-only discovery relay (no GPU, no wallet).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR btx-modelcheck (1),
.BR btx-open (1),
.BR btxd (1),
.I doc/modelnet/README.md
